<title>INDIA: INDIA NALCO SEEKS ALLOY WHEEL TECHNOLOGY.</title>
<headline>INDIA NALCO SEEKS ALLOY WHEEL TECHNOLOGY.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's state-run National Aluminium Company Ltd (NALCO) on Friday floated a global tender seeking technology to manufacture aluminium alloy wheels.</p>
<p>&quot;The company proposes to set up an aluminium wheel project for automobile industries comprising a 10,000 tonnes per annum wheel ingot line at its smelter plant at Angul and Chandaka, both in the (eastern) state of Orissa,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>NALCO is India's largest producer of aluminium.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91) 22-265 9000</p>
</text>
